  {
   "title": "Interpretation (LLM reasoning)",
   "text": "The docking and redocking results present a mixed picture. The redocking of the co-crystal ligand did not reproduce the original binding pose closely across the top-ranked mode, falling outside the range typically considered a successful self-docking validation, though a better-scoring alternate pose among the generated modes came closer to that threshold; this indicates the docking protocol's pose-reproduction reliability for this pocket is uncertain rather than confirmed. The enrichment metric suggests the scoring function has some ability to discriminate active from inactive compounds in this pocket, but it falls short of strong discriminatory performance. Given this, the binding score obtained for the docked ligand should be treated as a weak and uncertain indicator of binding preference rather than a validated measure, and it does not by itself support any conclusion about whether the ligand binds effectively, how it compares to other candidates, or whether the interaction would translate into any biological or therapeutic effect.\n\n*This paragraph is LLM reasoning over the findings above. It is tagged HYPOTHESIS: it contains no numbers of its own and was itself checked against the claims ledger before publication.*",
